 "summary": "Hilbert numbers and their s-number properties are new material; the proofs reuse the existing approximation-number calculus (`singularValue_comp_comp_le`, `singularValue_smul`, `singularValue_id`, `singularValue_eq_zero_of_rank_le`) and Mathlib's `LinearMap.isometryOfOrthonormal`/`exists_dual_vector''` rather than re-deriving them. The per-family `hilbertNumber_le_nnnorm`/`zero_hilbertNumber` overlap with `IsSNumberSequence.le_nnnorm`/`.zero` only in the monomorphic normed case and match the sibling Kolmogorov/Gelfand/Bernstein APIs in seminormed, universe-polymorphic generality.",
